<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Automata Scripting Prompt</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The second prompt (Listing <a href="#LST2" title="Listing 2 ‣ A.2 Automata Scripting Prompt ‣ Appendix A Abridged Prompts ‣ Real-Time World Crafting: Generating Structured Game Behaviors from Natural Language with Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) is tailored to the cellular automata sandbox. It instructs the LLM to generate a behavior script using a node-based DSL with a strict, procedural structure. Unlike the spell DSL, the sequence of conditional checks and actions in this language is highly important to the final outcome.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST2" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 2: </span>Abridged Automata Scripting Prompt.</figcaption>
<div id="LST2.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
